  "name": "rust-phf",
  "description": "Rust-PHF is a library for generating efficient, immutable lookup tables at compile time using perfect hash functions. It implements the CHD algorithm to construct collision-free maps and sets that provide O(1) search performance with minimal memory overhead. The library utilizes Rust macros and compiler plugins to pre-compute hash states, enabling static initialization of optimized data structures for performance-critical applications.",
